      "text": "Access Control. Lost: $12.9 K"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On 9 November 2024, the X319 staking contract on BNB Chain was exploited due to a missing access control on its claimEther function, resulting in the unauthorized withdrawal of approximately $12,900 in funds. The claimEther function in X319's staking contract lacked proper access control, allowing any caller to withdraw native tokens from the contract."
